# Reply keyboard in private chats

The Chat Menu Button (`MenuButtonWebApp`) occupies the client menu icon. A hidden reply keyboard then has nothing to reopen it.

## Rule

In a private chat, do not leave an inline-only message as the last bot message without a reply keyboard still applied.

One message accepts either an inline keyboard or a reply keyboard, not both. Feedback buttons (👍/👎) and the main menu are two sends.

To refresh the menu without a visible message, use `_pulse_reply_keyboard` in `bot_helpers.py`. Do not `send_message` plus an immediate delete: the client drops the keyboard if the carrier disappears before it is applied. The helper disables draft FX and waits before `delete_chat_message(..., kind="bot_own")`.

## Also

- Build reply keyboards only via `_reply_keyboard` in `i18n.py` (`resize_keyboard=True`, `is_persistent=True`). Do not construct a non-persistent `ReplyKeyboardMarkup`.
- Do not send `ReplyKeyboardRemove` in private chats.
- **Groups/channels:** never attach the main reply menu. Clear sticky keyboards with `ReplyKeyboardRemove` on group replies (`reply_setup_private_only`, schedule `/when`/`day`/`week`) or `clear_group_reply_keyboard` when silent. Android clients keep a persistent keyboard until remove is applied; macOS may already have dropped it.
- Do not run `sendMessageDraft` / typing FX on a message that carries a `ReplyKeyboardMarkup` (`message_fx.py` already skips those).
- System DMs (admin broadcasts, Twitch/Cursor/PostHog status, beta announce): include the «main menu» inline button (`dm_menu` / `dm_main_menu_keyboard`). Tapping it sends `menu_main` with the reply keyboard. Do not pulse+delete after these DMs — Android drops the menu when the carrier is deleted. Other private DMs that end on inline buttons need the same button, a lasting reply keyboard, or a proven pulse.
